{# Widget "recent" — just arrived (FL·02).

   STATIC TWIN of files.widgets.js's `recent` entry. Rendered by BOTH the hub and
   the widget library.

   Ordered by ARRIVAL, which is the only ordering that answers "has the Eastgate
   patrol synced yet". Everywhere else on this hub the ordering is the day the
   picture was taken. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiStorage/files/_ui.html.twig' as ui %}
<div class="c" data-w="recent">
    <span class="tab">Just arrived<span class="src">&middot; newest first, by the time they reached us</span></span>
    <div class="f-grid" data-f-grid>
        {%- for file in recent -%}{{ ui.tile(file) }}{%- endfor -%}
    </div>
    {% if recent is empty %}<div class="f-empty"><b>Nothing has arrived yet</b>A file reaches this hub by being attached to a record, on that record&rsquo;s own page.</div>{% endif %}
    {# The only ordering that answers "did the patrol sync yet". Everywhere else on
       this hub the ordering is when the picture was TAKEN — a patrol out for three
       days syncs on the third, and its photographs belong to the days they were
       taken. #}
    <div class="use">Ordered by <b>when they got here</b> &middot; everywhere else the order is <b>when the picture was taken</b>.</div>
</div>